*.tif filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.asset filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# The CXR registries / palettes are 0.7-4.6 KB of plain YAML. LFS makes them undiffable (git diff
# shows only an oid change) and unmergeable (merge=lfs is whole-file ours-or-theirs), which is how a
# clobbered entry goes unnoticed. Take ONLY this folder back out of LFS; the big .asset files
# (terrains, lightmaps, font atlases) must stay in it.
#   !filter        -> unspecified, so no filter driver runs = out of LFS
#   !diff !merge   -> unspecified, so git's normal text diff + 3-way merge apply.
#                     NOT -diff/-merge: an explicitly UNSET diff/merge means "binary", the opposite.
#   -text          -> kept deliberately. These files are LF and core.autocrlf is true here, so
#                     dropping -text would have git check them out as CRLF and Unity rewrite them
#                     as LF, giving permanent phantom diffs.
unity/CXRBrownfield/Assets/Resources/*.asset !filter !diff !merge -text
